
CASE: interruption at mv, followed by git status and recovery.
warning: templates not found in /opt/homebrew/opt/git/share/git-core/templates
warning: templates not found in /opt/homebrew/opt/git/share/git-core/templates
fm-record: state=unchanged detail=setup
fm-record: state=committed-local commit=ddbfff2
pending=1
pending_since=1788730598
delivery=pending
pending_age_seconds=0

$ fm-record.sh checkpoint --reason teardown --required [injected mv failure]
fm-record: state=configuration-error detail=commit-publication
pending=2
delivery=pending
pending_since=1788730598
pending_age_seconds=2
exit=9; the new commit and prepared index remain recoverable.
$ git show HEAD:note.md
after

$ GIT_OPTIONAL_LOCKS=1 git status --porcelain
MM note.md
git status changed cached index bytes and preserved all staged entries.

$ fm-record.sh checkpoint --reason teardown --required [fault removed]
fm-record: state=unchanged commit=a9b0279
pending=2
delivery=pending
pending_since=1788730598
pending_age_seconds=3
Recovery kept the same commit, reconciled the index, and removed the completed journal.

CASE: recovery refuses actual user staging.
fm-record: state=configuration-error detail=commit-publication
pending=3
delivery=pending
pending_since=1788730598
pending_age_seconds=5
$ git diff --cached --name-status
A	user.md
$ fm-record.sh checkpoint --reason stow
fm-record: state=configuration-error detail=index-recovery
pending=3
delivery=pending
pending_since=1788730598
pending_age_seconds=5
exit=8; the user index remained byte-for-byte unchanged.
$ git show :user.md
user staging

